# x-desktop-adopt: apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts (hot file, applied by the wiring task)

Import, beside `import { onProtocolAttached, publishScreenSessions } from './protocol/screen-sessions-publish';`:

    import { adoptProfileIfBehind } from './protocol/profile-adopt';

Place: next to `onProtocolAttached(localProtocol, refreshCorePageOrigin);` (the line that runs a function at each attach of
the local core's link). Add, for the local protocol only (a server's core is not this PC's profile):

    onProtocolAttached(localProtocol, () => {
      void adoptProfileIfBehind(localProtocol, app.getPath('userData'));
    });

`localProtocol` must offer `call(method, params)` (ProtocolConnection's `call`; `ProfileAdoptClient` needs only that).
adoptProfileIfBehind logs its failures at error level and never throws, so no catch is needed. After a successful
adopt the core reads the moved files (ssh hosts) itself: no core restart.

Core side: nothing. `migrate/profile/status` and `migrate/profile/adopt` are served by the migrate_profile domain already
(not in SERVICE_PENDING as far as read; the lead checks compose_flip.rs).
